

function plumed_preliminary_test(){
# check if the README.txt contains the word NAMD
  grep -q NAMD README.txt 1>/dev/null 2>/dev/null && test -f */Make.config
}

function plumed_patch_info(){
cat << EOF

To enable PLUMED in a NAMD simulation one should add the following lines in the NAMD configuration file
(often named as xxx.namd or xxx.conf) and run the plumed-patched version of NAMD with it:

\verbatim
plumed on
plumedfile plumed.dat
\endverbatim

The first line tells NAMD to run with PLUMED and the second line specifies the PLUMED input file.

Differently from the patches for older NAMD versions, this patch passes to PLUMED
the instantaneous cell and passes back to NAMD the PLUMED virial, so that constant pressure
simulations are possible. The energy of the PLUMED bias is reported in the MISC column
of the NAMD output and it is thus included in the total energy.

PLUMED can be used also in the GPU-resident mode of NAMD 3 ("GPUresident on"). As for Colvars and TclForces,
at every step the positions are copied from the GPU and the forces of PLUMED are copied to the GPU:
this has a cost also at the steps where PLUMED has nothing to compute.

\warning The experimental "SOAintegrate on" option of the CPU version is not supported:
in that case NAMD falls back to its standard integrator.

For more information on NAMD you should visit http://www.ks.uiuc.edu/Research/namd/

EOF
}

plumed_ignore_mpi=yes

